--> RNNs are not able to remember hidden memory states when context keeps increasing ,this is due to vanishing gradients for farer words

according to reasearchersnfor solving this problem , researchers introduced two beasts 

** LSTMS - Long Short term memory

** GRUS - Gated Recurrent Units

these architecture introduced so called GATES
basically , keeping a gate which is a Neural Net which decides which to take
as input , which to forget and which to output to hidden and cell states

--> a cell state type of nuance has been introduced in LSTM networks.
and this was the take for solving the memory problem
this cell state carrys information from past sentences and make the model remember the past information. 

--> then comes GRU , this architecture made for simplifying LSTM nets
basically this architecture completely removed the cell state and wants to make the lstm architecture phenomena in simple architecture but was in comparison similiar to lstm performance only!

the big and import problem have'nt been solved yet , which is parallel computation of weights and biases through the network , for scalability
means that these 3 architectures were not able to calculate the weights and biases parallely as the data moves sequentially and this was the primary bottleneck!

